# Hue app modeling

Rooms and zones belong to `HueApp`. Do not add an opt-in such as `roomsAndZones`. Callers do not turn the feature on. A gateway without area methods stays lights-only.

Sort rooms and zones in `@huxel/app`, in the area collection. UI sections render the order they are given.

Model behavior with classes and private state, as `LiveSync`, `AreaSync`, and `HueClientGateway` do. Do not build a feature as a closure that returns a bag of functions, or as a pile of free functions sharing mutable maps.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
export function createAreaEventSession(client, emit) {
	const pending = new Map();
	return { handle() {}, stop() {} };
}

// ✅ GOOD
export class AreaEventSession {
	private readonly pending = new Map<string, PendingAdd>();

	constructor(
		private readonly client: AreaClient,
		private readonly emit: (changes: AreaChange[]) => void
	) {}

	handle(): AreaChange[] {}
	stop(): void {}
}
```

Tests in `packages/app` fake `HueClient` with `FakeHueClient`. HTTP request mocking belongs in `@huxel/client`, not in `@huxel/app` gateway tests.
